  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening citizen participation in devolved governance for peace and sustainable development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This two-year project aims to improve the income-generation opportunities for youth and women, and to enhance community peace-building and cohesion in the face of tribalised politics, historical border and resource-based conflicts, in the counties of Kisumu, Kericho, Vihiga and Nandi. 

Building on an earlier project, Uhai lake Forum (ULF) will:
- Train 3 youth and 3 women&#x2019;s groups on income-generating activities, as well as entrepreneurship and marketing skills;
- Form and train 7 community education and leadership teams (CELTs) in community policing activities, as well as peacekeeping initiatives such as inter-ethnic sporting contests and leadership and peacebuilding activities in local schools;
- Provide capacity strengthening to the 7 CELTs in the form of training on county governance, constitution, public finance management, public expenditure monitoring, social accountability approaches (social auditing), advocacy and documentation; all with a view to undertaking a social audit process in order to engage with the county governments.</narrative>
  </description>
